  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The six-point star concentrates all its increases at six positions by working three "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "treble"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "trebles"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " into the leading stitch of each point column on every round, letting all other stitches stay at one. The points project clearly by round 3 and are fully defined by round 4. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "blocking"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "Blocking"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " with a pin at the tip of each point is essential: the yarn wants to round the points unless it is pinned and dried under tension."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "infoPanel",
        "attrs": {
          "variant": "materials"
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Yarn: DK weight cotton, approximately 30 m per motif. Hook: 4 mm. Notions: tapestry needle, scissors, blocking mat, 6 blocking pins (one per point)."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Gauge"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "4 rounds in DK cotton with a 4 mm hook = 14 cm point-to-point after blocking. Before blocking the points may measure only 11 cm; pinning each point individually under tension corrects this."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Stitches used"
          }
        ]
      },
